                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b74d8979-17e5-44c4-91ae-5cf5b55adec1",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c773b6d-46be-34d3-ae6f-16870b301f00",
                        "source_sense_id": "9d5f5a13-b307-3639-ba8b-3a6e4a15eca0",
                        "target_lang_word": "anvil",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anvil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                        "entry_id": "57caed26-0df8-3d4a-a18c-74539d7ca153",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A heavy iron block used in the blacksmithing trade as a surface upon which metal can be struck and shaped."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c0dfac1-ac18-480e-afd7-af2843e4a194",
                                                "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                                "text": "My heart is as an anvil unto sorrow,\nWhich beats upon it like the Cyclops’ hammers […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38fa9268-c0f9-4b6a-9d33-8d48930dd235",
                                                "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                                "text": "I saw a smith stand with his hammer, thus,\nThe whilst his iron did on the anvil cool,\nWith open mouth swallowing a tailor’s news […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2166094-0d5c-4898-9bde-5062062383ed",
                                                "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                                "text": "1794, William Blake, “The Tyger,” lines 15-16,\nWhat the anvil? what dread grasp / Dare its deadly terrors clasp?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c7da5f5-292c-4f31-9a78-7b053a5702ab",
                                                "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                                "text": "Thus at the flaming forge of life / Our fortunes must be wrought; / Thus on its sounding anvil shaped / Each burning deed and thought!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c8f4b5e-dd4e-47d2-8703-c27d34253444",
                                                "sense_id": "04f00f87-30fb-3d9b-8c36-c0a1b38171af",
                                                "text": "With an anvil-ding / And with fire in him forge thy will / Or rather, rather then, stealing as Spring / Through him, melt him but master him still: [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74d24117-1c30-337d-93ca-78d010b1c3f7",
                                        "entry_id": "57caed26-0df8-3d4a-a18c-74539d7ca153",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The incus bone in the middle ear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36ea73c1-c893-3945-8a39-ad896702521c",
                                        "entry_id": "57caed26-0df8-3d4a-a18c-74539d7ca153",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stone or other hard surface used by a bird for breaking the shells of snails."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d27b0db-cd7b-369d-a156-f653169ae8bd",
                                        "entry_id": "57caed26-0df8-3d4a-a18c-74539d7ca153",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The non-moving surface of a micrometer against which the item to be measured is placed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3b9f67f-b41d-36ed-93c0-92f086627701",
                                        "entry_id": "57caed26-0df8-3d4a-a18c-74539d7ca153",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horizontal-topped mass of cloud, shaped like a blacksmith's anvil, that forms before a thunderstorm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "anvil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc63c9ac-4ea5-36e0-9d76-7720a8e59668",
                                        "entry_id": "9b804dd5-8d25-3c6e-b9fa-45cf2ddf3966",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fashion on, or as if on, an anvil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "often",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af6fba69-6b28-4c4d-9788-fb172b78cbdb",
                                                "sense_id": "fc63c9ac-4ea5-36e0-9d76-7720a8e59668",
                                                "text": "I Have anvil’d out this Iron Age,\nWhich I commit, not to your patronage,\nBut skill and Art […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7ecae0c-cac9-4c25-805a-485a7e32daec",
                                                "sense_id": "fc63c9ac-4ea5-36e0-9d76-7720a8e59668",
                                                "text": "The Family Tang caus’d an Iron Pillar to be erected there of three Rods high, and of a proportionable thickness, Anvil’d out of an intire Piece."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de201b0d-168d-42d7-b1a5-7c8f8ad33d9c",
                                                "sense_id": "fc63c9ac-4ea5-36e0-9d76-7720a8e59668",
                                                "text": "I never started a roguery, that did not come out of thy forge in a manner ready anvilled and hammered for execution […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
